{"schema_version":"1.0","post_id":"2116129269642625233","post_url":"https://x.com/FrankCurzio/status/2116129269642625233","author":"@FrankCurzio","posted_at":"2026-10-30T11:25:08Z","collected_at":"2026-10-30T22:10:00+09:00","collected_by":"grok-automation/daily-us","text":"1. Coppernico ( $CPPMF ) - $0.27\n\nA copper explorer worth about $50M, with a 57,000-hectare land package in southern Peru (TSX: COPR).\n\nPeru approved its bigger drill permit in August, and Teck and Newmont are both shareholders.\n\nI own it, and I think it's a steal here.","post_type":"thread","in_reply_to_id":null,"thread_root_id":"2116128988393574431","quoted_post_id":null,"quoted_text":null,"edited":false,"media_note":"video discussing Coppernico stock","link_urls":[],"tickers_hint":["CPPMF"],"engagement":{"likes":3,"reposts":0,"replies":1,"views":334}}
{"schema_version":"1.0","post_id":"2116129310469992616","post_url":"https://x.com/FrankCurzio/status/2116129310469992616","author":"@FrankCurzio","posted_at":"2026-10-30T11:25:18Z","collected_at":"2026-10-30T22:10:00+09:00","collected_by":"grok-automation/daily-us","text":"2. Uranium Energy ( $UEC ) - $8.34\n\nOne of America's biggest uranium miners, producing in Texas and Wyoming with $495M in cash and no debt.\n\nIt's fallen from $20 back to $8.\n\nUranium stocks are rentals. You rent them when they're crushed like this, and sell into the big runs.","post_type":"thread","in_reply_to_id":null,"thread_root_id":"2116128988393574431","quoted_post_id":null,"quoted_text":null,"edited":false,"media_note":"video on UEC","link_urls":[],"tickers_hint":["UEC"],"engagement":{"likes":3,"reposts":0,"replies":1,"views":345}}
{"schema_version":"1.0","post_id":"2116129347300110645","post_url":"https://x.com/FrankCurzio/status/2116129347300110645","author":"@FrankCurzio","posted_at":"2026-10-30T11:25:26Z","collected_at":"2026-10-30T22:10:00+09:00","collected_by":"grok-automation/daily-us","text":"3. Uranium Royalty ( $UROY ) - $3.57\n\nIt doesn't mine. It pays miners upfront for a cut of what they produce, and it's now the biggest public landowner in Wyoming.\n\nI got in at 25 cents years ago and made a lot of money.\n\nThe cash keeps coming in without the drilling risk.","post_type":"thread","in_reply_to_id":null,"thread_root_id":"2116128988393574431","quoted_post_id":null,"quoted_text":null,"edited":false,"media_note":"video on UROY","link_urls":[],"tickers_hint":["UROY"],"engagement":{"likes":3,"reposts":0,"replies":1,"views":599}}
